ity of Nice, I entered the Universitat Autònoma de Barcelona as a “Ramón y Cajal” fellow, later becoming an associate professor there.\n\n### Research lines\n\nMy research belongs to the field of Algebraic Geometry, especially Interpolation in several variables, Singularities and related questions. I contributed to the Nagata and Segre-Harbourne-Gimigliano-Hirshowitz conjectures, to the study of degeneration of singularities and zerodiemensional schemes, Hilbert schemes and Seshadri constants, among others. At present I am interested in Nonarchimedean Analytic Geometry and Tropical Geometry.\n\n### Selected publications\n\n  * Maximal rank for schemes of small multiplicity by Évain’s differential Horace method. Trans. Amer. Math. Soc. 366 (2014), 857–874\n  * Variations on Nagata’s conjecture (j.w. C. Ciliberto, B. Harbourne and R. Miranda). In “A Celebration of Algebraic Geometry”, Brendan Hassett, James McKernan, Jason Starr i Ravi Vakil, editors; Clay Mathematics Proceedings 18 (2013)\n  * Iterated inverse images of plane curve singularities (j.w. E. Casas-Alvero). Acta Math. Sinica 27:12 (2011), 2319–2328\n  * An inequality between multipoint Seshadri constants (j.w. J. Ross). Geometriae Dedicata 140 (2009), 175–181\n  * Conditions imposed by tacnodes and cusps. Trans. Amer. Math. Soc. 353 (2001), 4925-4948\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nClay Mathematics Proceedings (https://www.math.colostate.edu/~miranda/preprints/cmip419.pdf)\nciteturn1search14 [wordlim: 200] Published: 5 months ago; CIRO CILIBERTO, BRIAN HARBOURNE, RICK MIRANDA, AND JOAQUIM RO´E ... , Nagata’s conjecture for a square or nearly-square number of points, Ric. ... Ross, An inequality between multipoint Seshadri constants, Geom.\npublished 2005. MR2202258 (2006k:14009)\n20. A. Hirschowitz, Une conjecture pour la cohomologie des diviseurs sur les surfaces rationelles\ng´en´eriques, J. Reine Angew. Math., 397 (1989), 208-213. MR993223 (90g:1402